<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB's Meyer sees Swiss M2 growth slowing in 1997.</title>
<headline>SNB's Meyer sees Swiss M2 growth slowing in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss National Bank chairman Hans Meyer said the M2 monetary aggregate grew an annual 10.3 percent in October but would slow down in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;In line with the policy that we envision, the growth of M2 money supply, which was 10.3 percent in October 1996, will clearly flatten out,&quot; Meyer said in a speech about 1997 policy and targets released before a news conference.</p>
</text>
